window.LEARN_CONTENT=window.LEARN_CONTENT||{};window.LEARN_CONTENT["a-dd3c07a3ae6aafeb"]={"zh":"<h1 id=\"mcp\">模型上下文协议（MCP）</h1> <blockquote> <p>完整文档索引请参阅 <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt（需联网）</a>。如需查看文档的 Markdown 版本，可在页面 URL 末尾追加 <code>.md</code>。</p> </blockquote> <p>模型上下文协议（MCP）让 ChatGPT 和 Codex 可以使用其他系统中的工具和信息。MCP 服务器会说明有哪些工具可用并处理工具请求，例如查询工单或检索文档。</p> <p>请选择适合你任务的方式：</p> <ul> <li><strong>创建连接：</strong>使用 <a href=\"#/article/a-dd3c07a3ae6aafeb?anchor=build-an-mcp-plugin\">Plugin Creator 和 Sites</a>为团队系统创建插件。</li> <li><strong>使用现有服务器：</strong><a href=\"#/article/a-dd3c07a3ae6aafeb?anchor=connect-an-existing-mcp-server\">将其连接到 ChatGPT 或 Codex</a>，并选择适用于网页、桌面应用、CLI 或 IDE 的设置方式。</li> </ul> <figure> <p class=\"media-note\">关于工单 123 的问题从 ChatGPT 经 MCP 服务器传递到工单系统。结果通过服务器返回，ChatGPT 随后报告该工单处于未结状态。 · <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://developers.openai.com/images/codex/custom-mcp/how-a-request-works-poster.webp\">联网查看原始媒体</a></p> <figcaption>关于工单 123 的问题从 ChatGPT 经 MCP 服务器传递到工单系统。结果通过服务器返回，ChatGPT 随后报告该工单处于未结状态。 · <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/images/codex/custom-mcp/how-a-request-works-poster.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">打开官网原始媒体</a></figcaption> </figure> <p><em>示例：在团队的支持系统中查看工单。</em></p> <p>插件将 MCP 连接打包起来，供 ChatGPT 使用。插件还可以包含可重复使用的技能指令。如果你只需要指令，请参阅<a href=\"#/article/a-0d81218eacd2463c\">构建插件</a>。</p> <p><a id=\"build-an-mcp-plugin\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"plugin-creator-sites-mcp\">使用 Plugin Creator 和 Sites 构建 MCP 插件</h2> <p>使用 Plugin Creator 创建和编辑插件，并通过 <a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/20001547-hosting-a-plugin-with-chatgpt-sites\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Sites（需联网）</a>托管其 MCP 服务器。</p> <h3 id=\"_1\">开始之前</h3> <p>请先查看<a href=\"https://chatgpt.com/plugins\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">插件目录（需联网）</a>。如果需要创建新连接，请准备好系统的 API 文档和经批准的连接方式。如需帮助，请联系系统所有者。</p> <p>以下示例将创建一个<strong>支持工单查询</strong>插件。请将 <strong>[工单系统]</strong>替换为你所用系统的名称。</p> <p><a id=\"chatgpt-enterprise\"></a> <strong>使用 ChatGPT Enterprise？</strong></p> <p>请工作区所有者或管理员检查<strong>工作区设置 → 权限与角色</strong>：</p> <ul> <li><strong>Use plugins（使用插件）</strong>：用于创建、编辑和使用插件。编辑插件还需要该插件的编辑权限。</li> <li><strong>Sites</strong>：用于创建和发布 Site。</li> <li><strong>Upload plugins（上传插件）</strong>和 <strong>Create plugins with MCPs（使用 MCP 创建插件）</strong>：授予发布 MCP 插件的 Site 所有者。</li> </ul> <p><strong>Use plugins（使用插件）</strong>默认开启；另外两项 MCP 发布权限默认关闭。请参阅 <a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/20001338-managing-chatgpt-sites-for-your-workspace\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Sites 访问权限（需联网）</a>和<a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/20001547-hosting-a-plugin-with-chatgpt-sites\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">插件权限（需联网）</a>。</p> <h3 id=\"1\">1. 创建插件</h3> <p>新建 Work 任务，选择 <strong>@Plugin Creator</strong>，并附上 API 文档。描述你的任务：</p> <p><strong>创建插件：</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Create a Support Ticket Lookup plugin with an MCP server hosted on Sites, using the attached [ticketing system] API docs. Let me look up a ticket's status, owner, and latest update by ticket number. Make it read-only and tell me what's needed to connect it.\n</code></pre><div class=\"prompt-translation\"><div class=\"prompt-reference-heading\"><strong>提示词中文参考</strong><button class=\"copy-code copy-prompt-translation\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"复制中文参考\">复制中文</button></div><div class=\"prompt-reference-text\">使用附带的 [ticketing system] API 文档，创建一个名为 Support Ticket Lookup 的插件，并将 MCP 服务器托管在 Sites 上。让我能够根据工单编号查询工单状态、负责人和最新更新。保持只读，并告诉我连接它需要哪些准备。</div></div> <p>如果 API 访问权限还未准备好，可以先让 Plugin Creator 使用示例数据。</p> <p><a id=\"connect-your-system\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"2\">2. 连接系统</h3> <p>在同一对话中，让 Plugin Creator 将服务器连接到系统 API，并引导你完成登录。请使用组织批准的身份验证方法，不要在聊天中透露密码、API 密钥或其他机密信息。</p> <p>需要帮助吗？将与 Plugin Creator 的对话和 API 文档发给系统所有者或开发者，请他们协助设置访问权限。</p> <p><strong>连接与托管详情</strong></p> <p>Sites 负责处理 ChatGPT 与 MCP 服务器之间的登录。你的服务器仍需通过获批的方式连接到系统 API；该 API 决定服务器可以访问哪些记录和执行哪些操作。</p> <p>如果使用其他主机，请按照<a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/plugins/build/mcp-server.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">构建 MCP 服务器</a>指南操作，然后<a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/plugins/deploy/connect-chatgpt.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">连接并测试插件</a>。登录设置请参阅<a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/plugins/build/auth.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">身份验证指南</a>。</p> <p><a id=\"connect-the-server-in-chatgpt\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"3\">3. 发布并安装</h3> <p>让 Plugin Creator 使用 Sites 发布服务器，并在保留当前访问设置的前提下提供插件链接。只有 <a href=\"#/article/a-fc9cd7880ec6ce59?anchor=_9\">Site 所有者可以发布（官网章节，需联网）</a> <a href=\"#/article/a-fc9cd7880ec6ce59\">本地页面（未识别该章节）</a>并创建对应插件；编辑者应请所有者代为操作。</p> <ol> <li>打开插件卡片，或在 <strong>Plugins（插件）→ Personal（个人）→ Created by you（由你创建）</strong>下找到插件。</li> <li>按照 <strong>Install（安装）</strong>和 <strong>Connect（连接）</strong>的提示操作，并完成必要的登录。</li> </ol> <h3 id=\"4\">4. 使用插件</h3> <p>新建 Work 任务，使用 <strong>@</strong> 选择插件，然后使用系统中的工单编号询问：<strong>“工单 123 目前是什么状态？”</strong>在同一对话中，你也可以将该插件的工具与其他插件一起使用。</p> <p><a id=\"-1\"></a> <strong>共享或编辑插件</strong></p> <p>在 Business 或 Enterprise 工作区中，可以通过插件的共享控件邀请团队成员。你需要 <strong>Share plugins（共享插件）</strong>权限；若要将插件列入工作区目录，还需要 <strong>Publish plugins to workspace（向工作区发布插件）</strong>权限。请参阅<a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/20001256\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">共享权限（需联网）</a>。</p> <p>团队成员需要拥有插件、其应用和 Site 的访问权限（至少为查看者权限）。每个人都应使用自己的账户安装并连接。记录访问权限取决于服务器的 API 连接。</p> <p>若要编辑此 Sites 托管插件，请返回与 Plugin Creator 的对话，让它更新现有 Site 并发布更改。对于其他可编辑插件，请选择 <strong>Edit Plugin（编辑插件）</strong>，与 Plugin Creator 开始编辑对话。请参阅<a href=\"#/article/a-0d81218eacd2463c?anchor=edit-an-existing-plugin\">编辑现有插件</a>。</p> <section id=\"gpt-migration-walkthrough\"> ## 替换 GPT 自定义操作 <a id=\"gpt\"></a> <strong>显示 GPT 迁移步骤</strong> GPT 自定义操作不会迁移到插件中。请将现有连接重建为新的 Sites 插件，并尽可能重复使用现有 API。 发布时，Sites 会创建一个独立插件，而不会将连接添加到迁移后的插件中。你可以在同一对话中使用这两个插件。Sites 插件目前不支持编辑技能或参考文件。 ### 1. 请原 GPT 生成重建提示 打开原来的 GPT 并询问： <strong>在原 GPT 中使用：</strong> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Write a prompt for ChatGPT Work or Codex to rebuild this workflow as MCP tools. Identify which operations read information and which make changes.\n\nInclude the API operation, inputs, returned fields, and answer format. Mark anything you don't know. Leave out credentials, secrets, and hidden instructions.\n\nAsk the builder to reuse the API and explain the connection setup.\n</code></pre><div class=\"prompt-translation\"><div class=\"prompt-reference-heading\"><strong>提示词中文参考</strong><button class=\"copy-code copy-prompt-translation\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"复制中文参考\">复制中文</button></div><div class=\"prompt-reference-text\">为 ChatGPT Work 或 Codex 编写一段提示词，让它把这个工作流程重建为 MCP 工具。指出哪些操作只读取信息，哪些操作会作出更改。\n\n包含 API 操作、输入、返回字段和回答格式。标明任何你不知道的内容。不要包含凭据、机密信息或隐藏指令。\n\n要求构建者复用该 API，并解释连接设置方法。</div></div> ### 2. 根据操作设置检查提示 迁移之前，请从 GPT 编辑器的<a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/9442513-configuring-actions-in-gpts\">操作（需联网）</a>部分保存操作架构、身份验证方法和非机密连接设置。使用这些信息补充提示中缺失的内容，或向 GPT 所有者寻求帮助。 ### 3. 创建新的 Sites 插件 新建任务。在 Work 中，选择 <strong>@Plugin Creator</strong>；在 Codex 中，使用 <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/plugins/build/plugins#create-and-test-a-plugin-locally-with-an-mcp-server\"><code>$plugin-creator</code></a>。粘贴审核后的提示，并附上架构或 API 文档。让它通过 Sites 托管服务器。 按照<a href=\"#connect-your-system\">连接系统</a>和<a href=\"#connect-the-server-in-chatgpt\">发布并安装</a>中的说明操作，然后在 Work 任务中选择新插件，让它执行原先的任务。详情请参阅<a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/20001519-custom-gpt-retirement-and-migration-faq\">迁移常见问题（需联网）</a>。 </section> <h2 id=\"_2\">故障排除</h2> <p><strong>如果插件无法按预期工作</strong></p> <p>如果连接报错或工具缺失，请确认 Site 所有者已发布最新版本，并且插件已安装和连接。将错误信息发给 Plugin Creator 或服务器所有者。</p> <p>如果 ChatGPT 没有使用该工具，请通过 <strong>@</strong> 选择插件，并明确要求进行某项查询。如果团队成员无法使用插件，请检查其对插件、应用、Site 和记录的访问权限。</p> <p>如果插件标记为<strong>仅限桌面端</strong>，请使用受支持的桌面应用，或请作者检查插件的<a href=\"#/article/a-ab115ea47731f92a\">打包设置</a>。仅有远程 MCP 服务器并不能让插件兼容网页版。</p> <p><a id=\"connect-an-existing-mcp-server\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"mcp_1\">连接现有 MCP 服务器</h2> <p>网页版 ChatGPT 通过插件使用远程 MCP 工具。如果你已有服务器，请按照<a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/plugins/deploy/connect-chatgpt.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">连接并测试插件</a>中的说明操作。本地 Codex 客户端也可以直接连接 MCP 服务器，并共享其配置。</p> <p>选择使用界面，查看相应的设置与配置选项。</p> <p><a id=\"supported-mcp-features\"></a></p> <blockquote> <p><strong>适用界面：app,cli,ide</strong></p> </blockquote> <p>ChatGPT 桌面应用、Codex CLI 和 IDE 扩展均支持 MCP 服务器，并共享同一 Codex 主机的 MCP 配置。</p> <p>以下受支持的服务器功能适用于在 Codex 主机上配置的 MCP 服务器。托管插件工具可能具有不同的能力。</p> <h2 id=\"mcp_2\">支持的 MCP 功能</h2> <ul> <li><strong>STDIO 服务器：</strong>作为本地进程运行（通过命令启动）的服务器。</li> <li>环境变量</li> <li><strong>可流式传输的 HTTP 服务器：</strong>通过地址访问的服务器。</li> <li>Bearer 令牌身份验证</li> <li>OAuth 身份验证，包括客户端 ID 元数据文档（CIMD）和动态客户端注册（DCR）</li> <li>对可信的第一方服务器使用 ChatGPT 会话身份验证</li> <li><strong>服务器指令：</strong>Codex 会读取初始化期间返回的 MCP <code>instructions</code> 字段，并将其与服务器工具一起作为适用于整个服务器的指导信息。</li> </ul> <p>如果你为 Codex 构建或维护 MCP 服务器，请使用 <code>instructions</code> 说明跨工具工作流、约束和适用于整个服务器的速率限制。请确保前 512 个字符内容完整自洽，以便 Codex 判断如何使用服务器时，能优先获得最重要的指导信息。</p> <h2 id=\"codex-mcp\">将 Codex 连接到 MCP 服务器</h2> <p>Codex 会将 MCP 配置与其他 Codex 配置一并保存在 <code>config.toml</code> 中。默认文件位置为 <code>~/.codex/config.toml</code>；也可以使用项目目录中的 <code>.codex/config.toml</code> 单独配置项目的 MCP 服务器（仅适用于受信任的项目）。</p> <p>ChatGPT 桌面应用、Codex CLI 和 IDE 扩展共享此配置。设置好 MCP 服务器后，你可以在这些客户端之间切换，而无需重复配置。</p> <blockquote> <p><strong>适用界面：app</strong></p> </blockquote> <h3 id=\"chatgpt\">在 ChatGPT 桌面应用中配置</h3> <ol> <li>打开 <strong>Settings（设置）</strong>，然后选择 <strong>MCP servers（MCP 服务器）</strong>。</li> <li>选择 <strong>Add server（添加服务器）</strong>。</li> <li>输入名称，选择 <strong>STDIO</strong> 或 <strong>Streamable HTTP（可流式传输的 HTTP）</strong>，并提供服务器命令或 URL。</li> <li>保存服务器，然后选择 <strong>Restart（重新启动）</strong>。</li> </ol> <p>服务器列表会显示已启用的服务器以及需要 OAuth 的服务器。OAuth 服务器要求登录时，请选择 <strong>Authenticate（身份验证）</strong>。在消息编辑框中输入 <code>/mcp</code> 可查看已连接的服务器。</p> <blockquote> <p><strong>适用界面：web</strong></p> </blockquote> <h2 id=\"chatgpt-mcp\">在网页版 ChatGPT 中使用基于 MCP 的工具</h2> <p>在其他设备上通过 Work Cloud 的本地计算机访问继续对话，不会安装插件，也不会授予对已连接账户的访问权限。</p> <p>在 Work Cloud 本地计算机访问模式中，Agent Security 中企业级 <code>mcp_servers</code> TOML 要求适用于本地执行器。云容器仍遵循 Work Cloud 策略。云端可能无法使用本地 MCP 服务器和传输方式；请分别检查连接和身份验证。</p> <p>在 Work Cloud 本地计算机访问模式中使用企业钩子时：</p> <ul> <li><strong>企业钩子。</strong>如果工作区启用了此功能，Work Cloud 本地计算机访问支持由管理员定义的 MCP 钩子。这些钩子会在云协调器（编排器）上响应受支持的生命周期事件和工具事件运行。即使工具在本地执行，命令钩子以及来自本地配置或插件的钩子也不支持云端编排。</li> <li><strong>审计。</strong>依赖这些钩子之前，请测试回调连接、确认其接收的事件，并检查钩子失败会如何影响任务。MCP 钩子无法提供完整的 Compliance API 审计记录。</li> <li><strong>限制：</strong>即使工具在本地执行，命令钩子以及来自本地配置或插件的钩子也不支持云端编排。此功能不向使用者提供钩子支持。当编排和执行都在本地进行时，现有受支持的钩子仍可在仅限本地的 Work 和 Codex 线程中使用。管理员仍可在 Agent Security 中为这些工作流配置受支持的托管钩子。</li> </ul> <p>有关支持范围，请参阅 <a href=\"#/article/a-0aecdb1ef0cec0a4\">Hooks</a>和<a href=\"#/article/a-c2332644faa13713\">配置参考</a>。</p> <p>在托管的 ChatGPT Work 聊天中，安装<a href=\"#/article/a-dea5d8982f047a3a\">插件</a>即可使用其内置连接器和远程 MCP 工具。安装后，Chat 和 Work 都可以使用这些工具。工作区管理员可以控制哪些插件和工具可用。</p> <p>网页版 ChatGPT 不会读取本地 Codex 配置文件，也不会显示本地 Codex 命令菜单。打开 <strong>Plugins（插件）</strong>标签页即可浏览和管理可用工具。</p> <blockquote> <p><strong>适用界面：cli</strong></p> </blockquote> <h3 id=\"cli\">使用 CLI 配置</h3> <h4 id=\"mcp_3\">添加 MCP 服务器</h4> <pre><code class=\"language-bash\">codex mcp add &lt;server-name&gt; --env VAR1=VALUE1 --env VAR2=VALUE2 -- &lt;stdio server-command&gt;\n</code></pre> <p>例如，若要添加 Context7（免费的开发者文档 MCP 服务器），可以运行以下命令：</p> <pre><code class=\"language-bash\">codex mcp add context7 -- npx -y @upstash/context7-mcp\n</code></pre> <h4 id=\"cli_1\">其他 CLI 命令</h4> <p>运行 <code>codex mcp list</code> 可查看已配置的服务器。若要查看所有可用的 MCP 命令，请运行 <code>codex mcp --help</code>。对于支持 OAuth 的服务器，请运行 <code>codex mcp login &lt;server-name&gt;</code>。</p> <h4 id=\"tui\">终端用户界面（TUI）</h4> <p>在 <code>codex</code> TUI 中，输入 <code>/mcp</code> 可查看当前启用的 MCP 服务器。</p> <blockquote> <p><strong>适用界面：ide</strong></p> </blockquote> <h3 id=\"ide\">在 IDE 扩展中配置</h3> <ol> <li>打开齿轮菜单，然后选择 <strong>MCP servers（MCP 服务器）</strong>。</li> <li>选择 <strong>Add server（添加服务器）</strong>。</li> <li>输入名称，选择 <strong>STDIO</strong> 或 <strong>Streamable HTTP（可流式传输的 HTTP）</strong>，并提供服务器命令或 URL。</li> <li>保存服务器，然后选择 <strong>Restart extension（重新启动扩展）</strong>。</li> </ol> <p>MCP 服务器列表会显示已启用的服务器以及需要 OAuth 的服务器。OAuth 服务器要求登录时，请选择 <strong>Authenticate（身份验证）</strong>。</p> <blockquote> <p><strong>适用界面：app,cli,ide</strong></p> </blockquote> <h3 id=\"configtoml\">使用 config.toml 配置</h3> <p>若要进行更精细的控制，请编辑 <code>~/.codex/config.toml</code> 或项目专用的 <code>.codex/config.toml</code>。有关所有受支持 MCP 选项的可搜索列表，请参阅<a href=\"#/article/a-c2332644faa13713\">配置参考</a>。</p> <p>在配置文件中使用 <code>[mcp_servers.&lt;server-name&gt;]</code> 表配置各个 MCP 服务器。</p> <p><a id=\"stdio-servers\"></a></p> <blockquote> <p><strong>适用界面：app,cli,ide</strong></p> </blockquote> <h4 id=\"stdio\">STDIO 服务器</h4> <ul> <li><code>command</code>（必需）：用于启动服务器的命令。</li> <li><code>args</code>（可选）：传递给服务器的参数。</li> <li><code>env</code>（可选）：为服务器设置的环境变量。</li> <li><code>env_vars</code>（可选）：允许使用并转发的环境变量。</li> <li><code>cwd</code>（可选）：启动服务器时使用的工作目录。</li> <li><code>experimental_environment</code>（可选）：如果远程执行器环境可用，将其设为 <code>remote</code>，即可通过该环境启动 stdio 服务器。</li> </ul> <p><code>env_vars</code> 可以包含普通变量名，也可以包含指定来源的对象：</p> <pre><code class=\"language-toml\">env_vars = [\"LOCAL_TOKEN\", { name = \"REMOTE_TOKEN\", source = \"remote\" }]\n</code></pre> <p>字符串条目和 <code>source = \"local\"</code> 会从 Codex 本地环境读取变量。<code>source = \"remote\"</code> 会从远程执行器环境读取变量，并要求使用远程 MCP stdio。</p> <p><a id=\"streamable-http-servers\"></a></p> <blockquote> <p><strong>适用界面：app,cli,ide</strong></p> </blockquote> <h4 id=\"http\">可流式传输的 HTTP 服务器</h4> <ul> <li><code>url</code>（必需）：服务器地址。</li> <li><code>auth</code>（可选）：在已配置的 Bearer 令牌和授权标头之后尝试的身份验证方式。使用 <code>oauth</code>（默认值）可使用已存储的 MCP OAuth 凭据。使用 <code>chatgpt</code> 可在受信任的第一方 ChatGPT 来源中使用当前 ChatGPT 会话；如果不可用，则回退到已存储的 OAuth 凭据。</li> <li><code>bearer_token_env_var</code>（可选）：要在 <code>Authorization</code> 中发送的 Bearer 令牌所对应的环境变量名称。</li> <li><code>http_headers</code>（可选）：将标头名称映射到静态值。</li> <li><code>env_http_headers</code>（可选）：将标头名称映射到环境变量名称（值从环境中读取）。</li> <li><code>http_headers_helper</code>（可选）：本地命令，用于输出包含标头名称和字符串值的 JSON 对象，例如 <code>{\"X-Auth\": \"temporary-token\"}</code>。仅支持从本地环境发起的 HTTP MCP 连接；不支持 stdio 服务器，也不支持通过远程执行环境建立的连接。</li> </ul> <p>Codex 会缓存连接使用的辅助标头。当同源 POST 返回 <code>401</code> 或 <code>403</code> 时，Codex 会刷新一次标头；只有辅助程序返回的值发生变化时才会重试。明确配置的 Bearer 令牌和 OAuth 凭据优先级高于辅助程序提供的 <code>Authorization</code> 标头。如果 OAuth <code>403</code> 响应报告权限范围不足，则不会触发辅助程序刷新。</p> <p>如果无法解析任何凭据来源，Codex 可以在不进行身份验证的情况下连接服务器。请单独运行 <code>codex mcp login &lt;server-name&gt;</code>，以启动 MCP OAuth 登录。</p> <h4 id=\"_3\">其他配置选项</h4> <ul> <li><code>startup_timeout_sec</code>（可选）：服务器启动超时时间（秒）。默认值：<code>10</code>。</li> <li><code>tool_timeout_sec</code>（可选）：服务器运行工具的超时时间（秒）。默认值：<code>60</code>。</li> <li><code>enabled</code>（可选）：设为 <code>false</code>，即可停用服务器而不删除配置。</li> <li><code>required</code>（可选）：设为 <code>true</code> 后，如果此已启用的服务器无法初始化，Codex 将无法启动。</li> <li><code>enabled_tools</code>（可选）：工具允许列表。</li> <li><code>disabled_tools</code>（可选）：工具拒绝列表（在 <code>enabled_tools</code> 之后应用）。</li> <li><code>default_tools_approval_mode</code>（可选）：此服务器工具的默认审批行为。支持的值为 <code>auto</code>、<code>prompt</code>、<code>writes</code> 和 <code>approve</code>。<code>writes</code> 模式会针对未标记为只读的工具请求审批。</li> <li><code>tools.&lt;tool&gt;.approval_mode</code>（可选）：覆盖单个工具的审批行为。</li> <li><code>tools.&lt;tool&gt;.output_token_limit</code>（可选）：单个工具输出可使用的正整数 token 预算，不包括标准的 20% 序列化余量。此设置会覆盖模型针对该工具的默认输出截断预算。</li> </ul> <p>顶层设置 <code>mcp_optional_startup_grace_ms</code> 控制 Codex 构建初始工具目录时等待可选 MCP 服务器的时长。默认值为 <code>1000</code> 毫秒。将其设为 <code>0</code>，即可改为等待每个服务器的 <code>startup_timeout_sec</code>。必需服务器仍使用各自的启动超时时间。</p> <h4 id=\"oauth\">OAuth 客户端注册与回调</h4> <p>如果授权服务器要求预先注册 OAuth 客户端，请在添加 MCP 服务器时提供客户端 ID：</p> <pre><code class=\"language-bash\">codex mcp add example --url https://mcp.example.com --oauth-client-id my-client\n</code></pre> <p>对于机密客户端，还需传入 <code>--oauth-client-secret</code>。请从环境变量读取密钥：</p> <pre><code class=\"language-bash\">codex mcp add example --url https://mcp.example.com --oauth-client-id my-client --oauth-client-secret \"$MCP_CLIENT_SECRET\"\n</code></pre> <p>此选项要求客户端 ID 和密钥均非空。Codex 会在 <code>config.toml</code> 中将密钥保存为 <code>mcp_servers.example.oauth.client_secret</code>。请妥善保护此文件，并避免将其纳入版本控制。</p> <p>Codex 会显示完整回调 URL，供你在服务提供商处注册：</p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">OAuth callback URL: http://127.0.0.1/callback\n</code></pre> <p>Codex 会在 <code>config.toml</code> 中将回调地址与客户端 ID 一同保存，以供后续登录使用：</p> <pre><code class=\"language-toml\">[mcp_servers.example]\nurl = \"https://mcp.example.com\"\n\n[mcp_servers.example.oauth]\nclient_id = \"my-client\"\ncallback_url = \"http://127.0.0.1/callback\"\n</code></pre> <p>只有当授权服务器通过元数据声明 <code>authorization_response_iss_parameter_supported: true</code> 并提供 <code>issuer</code> 时，新添加的预注册客户端才会使用固定回调地址。如果元数据未声明支持 issuer，Codex 会追加服务器专用的回调 ID，例如 <code>http://127.0.0.1/callback/XuuuHAzzHOni</code>。尚未保存回调地址的现有客户端会继续使用带有各自回调 ID 的重定向地址。</p> <p>登录期间使用哪个回调地址，取决于 OAuth 配置和授权服务器元数据：</p> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>OAuth 配置</th> <th>Issuer 支持情况</th> <th>使用的回调地址</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td>配置了 <code>callback_url</code>，但未配置 <code>client_id</code></td> <td>支持</td> <td>使用已配置的回调地址注册客户端。</td> </tr> <tr> <td>配置了 <code>callback_url</code>，但未配置 <code>client_id</code></td> <td>不支持</td> <td>在已配置的回调地址后追加服务器专用回调 ID，再用于客户端注册。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>client_id</code> 和 <code>callback_url</code></td> <td>支持</td> <td>重用已配置的回调地址；授权响应必须包含匹配的 <code>iss</code>。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>client_id</code> 和以正确回调 ID 结尾的 <code>callback_url</code></td> <td>不支持</td> <td>原样重用已配置的回调地址。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>client_id</code> 和缺少正确回调 ID 的 <code>callback_url</code></td> <td>不支持</td> <td>忽略已配置的回调地址。Codex 使用 <code>mcp_oauth_callback_url</code>；如果未设置，则使用 <code>http://127.0.0.1/callback</code>，并追加回调 ID。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>client_id</code>，但未配置 <code>callback_url</code></td> <td>支持或不支持</td> <td>Codex 使用全局或默认回调地址，并追加服务器专用回调 ID。</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p>回退机制不会修改已存储的回调 URL。Codex 会根据 MCP 服务器 URL（包括其路径和查询字符串）推导回调 ID。自动登录和显式登录遵循相同的选择规则。</p> <p>如果需要自定义回调路径或远程 Devbox 入站 URL，请设置 <code>mcp_oauth_callback_url</code>。对于新添加的预注册客户端，如果其服务提供商支持 issuer 识别，则会原样使用此 URL；否则会在已配置的 URL 后追加服务器专用回调 ID。请务必注册 <code>codex mcp add</code> 显示的准确回调地址。</p> <p>对于未明确指定端口的 <code>http://127.0.0.1</code> 回调，Codex 在显示和存储的 URL 中省略监听端口，并在授权期间填入当前监听端口。此替换规则不适用于 <code>localhost</code>、IPv6 主机、HTTPS URL 或已包含端口的回调地址。根据 <a href=\"https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8252#section-7.3\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">RFC 8252 第 7.3 节（需联网）</a>，授权服务器必须接受可变的回环端口。</p> <p>设置 <code>mcp_oauth_callback_port</code> 可指定固定的全局监听端口；设置 <code>mcp_servers.&lt;server-name&gt;.oauth.callback_port</code> 可为单个服务器指定覆盖值。回调 URL 中显式指定的端口不会配置监听器。对于直接回环回调，请使用不带显式端口的 <code>http://127.0.0.1</code>，或为回调 URL 和监听器配置相同的显式端口。代理回调可以有意使用与本地监听端口不同的外部 URL 端口。本地回调 URL 绑定到本地接口；非本地回调 URL 则绑定到 <code>0.0.0.0</code>。</p> <p>Codex 会先验证响应中的 <code>iss</code>，再交换授权码。<code>iss</code> 不匹配时，一律拒绝该响应。如果元数据声明支持 issuer，但响应缺少 <code>iss</code>，也会拒绝该响应。这两种错误都不会交换授权码，也不会回退到其他回调地址。回调 URL 格式错误，或元数据声明支持 issuer 却未提供 issuer 值，同样会导致硬性失败。请参阅<a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/plugins/build/auth.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">用户身份验证</a>。</p> <p>如果 MCP 服务器声明了 <code>scopes_supported</code>，Codex 在 OAuth 登录时会优先采用服务器声明的权限范围；否则会回退到 <code>config.toml</code> 中配置的权限范围。</p> <h4 id=\"oauth_1\">OAuth 客户端注册</h4> <p>Codex 支持 <a href=\"https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/draft-ietf-oauth-client-id-metadata-document/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">OAuth 客户端 ID 元数据文档（CIMD）（需联网）</a>和动态客户端注册（DCR）。默认情况下，如果授权服务器通过元数据声明 <code>client_id_metadata_document_supported: true</code>，在 <code>token_endpoint_auth_methods_supported</code> 中包含 <code>none</code>，且回调使用受支持的回环 URL，Codex 会自动选择 CIMD。否则，如果 DCR 可用，则使用 DCR。已配置的 OAuth 客户端 ID 始终优先，并会跳过客户端注册。</p> <p>对于不支持绑定 issuer 的响应的 CIMD，Codex CLI 会使用 ChatGPT 托管的、针对该 MCP 服务器的元数据文档：</p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">https://chatgpt.com/oauth/codex/&lt;callback_id&gt;/client.json\n</code></pre> <p>Codex 会根据 MCP 服务器 URL 推导 <code>&lt;callback_id&gt;</code>，并将其包含在回环重定向 URI 中，例如 <code>http://127.0.0.1:&lt;port&gt;/callback/&lt;callback_id&gt;</code>。元数据文档会注册相应的不带端口的回环 URI。根据 <a href=\"https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8252.html#section-7.3\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">RFC 8252（需联网）</a>，授权服务器必须接受登录时选择的端口，同时严格匹配主机和路径。自定义回调主机、路径或查询参数需要使用 DCR 或已配置的 OAuth 客户端 ID。</p> <p>Codex CLI 还支持固定且共享的 CIMD 文档：</p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">https://chatgpt.com/oauth/codex/client.json\n</code></pre> <p>Codex CLI 会在以下条件全部满足时，使用带有共享 <code>/callback</code> 路径的固定文档：授权服务器声明 <code>authorization_response_iss_parameter_supported: true</code>、在元数据中提供有效的 <code>issuer</code>，并在授权响应中包含匹配的 <code>iss</code>。不支持绑定 issuer 的响应的服务器则使用专用回调文档。</p> <p>若要为单次 CLI 登录选择注册方式，请使用 <code>--oauth-client-registration</code>：</p> <pre><code class=\"language-bash\">codex mcp login &lt;server-name&gt; --oauth-client-registration cimd\ncodex mcp login &lt;server-name&gt; --oauth-client-registration dcr\n</code></pre> <p>默认值为 <code>auto</code>。注册方式的选择仅对当前登录有效，不会保存在 <code>config.toml</code> 中。</p> <h4 id=\"configtoml_1\">config.toml 示例</h4> <pre><code class=\"language-toml\">[mcp_servers.context7]\ncommand = \"npx\"\nargs = [\"-y\", \"@upstash/context7-mcp\"]\nenv_vars = [\"LOCAL_TOKEN\"]\n\n[mcp_servers.context7.env]\nMY_ENV_VAR = \"MY_ENV_VALUE\"\n</code></pre> <pre><code class=\"language-toml\"># Optional MCP OAuth callback overrides (used by `codex mcp login`)\nmcp_oauth_callback_port = 5555\nmcp_oauth_callback_url = \"https://devbox.example.internal/callback\"\n</code></pre> <pre><code class=\"language-toml\">[mcp_servers.figma]\nurl = \"https://mcp.figma.com/mcp\"\nbearer_token_env_var = \"FIGMA_OAUTH_TOKEN\"\nhttp_headers = { \"X-Figma-Region\" = \"us-east-1\" }\n</code></pre> <pre><code class=\"language-toml\">[mcp_servers.chrome_devtools]\nurl = \"http://localhost:3000/mcp\"\nenabled_tools = [\"open\", \"screenshot\"]\ndisabled_tools = [\"screenshot\"] # applied after enabled_tools\ndefault_tools_approval_mode = \"prompt\"\nstartup_timeout_sec = 20\ntool_timeout_sec = 45\nenabled = true\n\n[mcp_servers.chrome_devtools.tools.open]\napproval_mode = \"approve\"\noutput_token_limit = 30000\n</code></pre> <h3 id=\"mcp_4\">插件提供的 MCP 服务器</h3> <p>已安装的插件可以在插件清单中包含 MCP 服务器。这些服务器由插件启动，因此用户配置无需为其指定传输命令。用户仍可通过 <code>plugins.&lt;plugin&gt;.mcp_servers.&lt;server&gt;</code> 控制启用状态和工具策略。</p> <pre><code class=\"language-toml\">[plugins.\"sample@test\".mcp_servers.sample]\nenabled = true\ndefault_tools_approval_mode = \"prompt\"\nenabled_tools = [\"read\", \"search\"]\n\n[plugins.\"sample@test\".mcp_servers.sample.tools.search]\napproval_mode = \"approve\"\n</code></pre> <p>插件提供的 HTTP MCP 服务器也可以在 <code>.mcp.json</code> 中声明 OAuth 设置。插件清单使用驼峰式字段名称 <code>clientId</code>、<code>callbackUrl</code> 和 <code>callbackPort</code>：</p> <pre><code class=\"language-json\">{\n  \"mcpServers\": {\n    \"sample\": {\n      \"type\": \"http\",\n      \"url\": \"https://mcp.example.com/mcp\",\n      \"oauth\": {\n        \"clientId\": \"my-pre-registered-client\",\n        \"callbackUrl\": \"http://127.0.0.1/callback/registered\"\n      }\n    }\n  }\n}\n</code></pre> <p>插件提供的 MCP 服务器遵循与其他 MCP 服务器相同的回调地址选择规则。如果插件提供了 <code>clientId</code>，但其服务提供商不支持绑定 issuer 的回调，且 <code>callbackUrl</code> 缺少服务器专用回调 ID，则 Codex 会在登录时忽略该 URL，并使用 <code>mcp_oauth_callback_url</code>；如果未设置，则使用 <code>http://127.0.0.1/callback</code> 并追加回调 ID。已配置的 <code>callbackUrl</code> 不会被更改。</p> <p>插件的 <code>oauth.callbackPort</code> 会覆盖全局设置 <code>mcp_oauth_callback_port</code>；如果两者都未设置，Codex 会选择一个临时端口。<code>callbackUrl</code> 中的端口不会决定监听器端口。对于使用固定端口的直接回环回调，请将两个值配置为一致：</p> <pre><code class=\"language-json\">{\n  \"callbackUrl\": \"http://127.0.0.1:4321/callback/registered\",\n  \"callbackPort\": 4321\n}\n</code></pre> <p>对于远程入站或其他代理，如果代理会将请求转发到已配置的监听器，则回调 URL 端口可以有意设置为与本地监听端口不同。</p> <h2 id=\"mcp_5\">实用 MCP 服务器示例</h2> <p>MCP 服务器的种类不断增加。以下是一些常见示例：</p> <ul> <li><a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/learn/docs-mcp.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">OpenAI Docs MCP</a>：搜索并阅读 OpenAI 开发者文档。</li> <li><a href=\"https://github.com/upstash/context7\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Context7（需联网）</a>：连接到保持最新的开发者文档。</li> <li>Figma <a href=\"https://developers.figma.com/docs/figma-mcp-server/local-server-installation/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">本地版（需联网）</a>和<a href=\"https://developers.figma.com/docs/figma-mcp-server/remote-server-installation/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">远程版（需联网）</a>：访问你的 Figma 设计。</li> <li><a href=\"https://www.npmjs.com/package/@playwright/mcp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Playwright（需联网）</a>：使用 Playwright 控制和检查浏览器。</li> <li><a href=\"https://github.com/ChromeDevTools/chrome-devtools-mcp/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Chrome Developer Tools（需联网）</a>：控制和检查 Chrome。</li> <li><a href=\"https://docs.sentry.io/product/sentry-mcp/#codex\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Sentry（需联网）</a>：访问 Sentry 日志。</li> <li><a href=\"https://github.com/github/github-mcp-server\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">GitHub（需联网）</a>：执行 <code>git</code> 不支持的 GitHub 管理任务，例如处理拉取请求和问题。</li> </ul>","en":"<h1 id=\"model-context-protocol\">Model Context Protocol</h1> <blockquote> <p>For the complete documentation index, see <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt (online)</a>. Markdown versions of documentation pages are available by appending <code>.md</code> to the page URL.</p> </blockquote> <p>Model Context Protocol (MCP) lets ChatGPT and Codex use tools and information from other systems. An MCP server describes the available tools and handles their requests—for example, looking up a ticket or retrieving documentation.</p> <p>Choose the path that fits your task:</p> <ul> <li><strong>Build a connection:</strong> Use <a href=\"#/article/a-dd3c07a3ae6aafeb?anchor=build-an-mcp-plugin-with-plugin-creator-and-sites\">Plugin Creator and Sites</a> to create a plugin for your team's system.</li> <li><strong>Use an existing server:</strong> <a href=\"#/article/a-dd3c07a3ae6aafeb?anchor=connect-an-existing-mcp-server\">Connect it to ChatGPT or Codex</a>, with setup options for web, desktop, CLI, and IDE.</li> </ul> <figure> <p class=\"media-note\">A question about ticket 123 passes from ChatGPT through the MCP server to the ticketing system. The result returns through the server, and ChatGPT reports that the ticket is open. · <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://developers.openai.com/images/codex/custom-mcp/how-a-request-works-poster.webp\">联网查看原始媒体</a></p> <figcaption>A question about ticket 123 passes from ChatGPT through the MCP server to the ticketing system. The result returns through the server, and ChatGPT reports that the ticket is open. · <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/images/codex/custom-mcp/how-a-request-works-poster.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Open original media</a></figcaption> </figure> <p><em>Example: checking a ticket in your team's support system.</em></p> <p>A plugin packages an MCP connection for use in ChatGPT. Plugins can also contain skills with reusable instructions. If you only need instructions, see <a href=\"#/article/a-0d81218eacd2463c\">Build plugins</a>.</p> <h2 id=\"build-an-mcp-plugin-with-plugin-creator-and-sites\">Build an MCP plugin with Plugin Creator and Sites</h2> <p>Use Plugin Creator to create and edit your plugin, and <a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/20001547-hosting-a-plugin-with-chatgpt-sites\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Sites (online)</a> to host its MCP server.</p> <h3 id=\"before-you-start\">Before you start</h3> <p>Check the <a href=\"https://chatgpt.com/plugins\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Plugins directory (online)</a> first. If you need a new connection, gather your system's API documentation and an approved way to connect. Ask the system owner if you need help.</p> <p>The example below creates a <strong>Support Ticket Lookup</strong> plugin. Replace <strong>[ticketing system]</strong> with your system's name.</p> <p><a id=\"using-chatgpt-enterprise\"></a> <strong>Using ChatGPT Enterprise?</strong></p> <p>Ask your workspace owner or admin to check <strong>Workspace settings → Permissions &amp; roles</strong>:</p> <ul> <li><strong>Use plugins</strong> to create, edit, and use plugins. Editing also requires edit access to the plugin.</li> <li><strong>Sites</strong> access to create and publish your Site.</li> <li><strong>Upload plugins</strong> and <strong>Create plugins with MCPs</strong> for the Site owner who publishes the MCP-backed plugin.</li> </ul> <p><strong>Use plugins</strong> is on by default; the two MCP publishing permissions are off by default. See <a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/20001338-managing-chatgpt-sites-for-your-workspace\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Sites access (online)</a> and <a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/20001547-hosting-a-plugin-with-chatgpt-sites\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">plugin permissions (online)</a>.</p> <h3 id=\"1-create-your-plugin\">1. Create your plugin</h3> <p>Start a new Work task, select <strong>@Plugin Creator</strong>, and attach your API documentation. Describe the task:</p> <p><strong>Create your plugin:</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Create a Support Ticket Lookup plugin with an MCP server hosted on Sites, using the attached [ticketing system] API docs. Let me look up a ticket's status, owner, and latest update by ticket number. Make it read-only and tell me what's needed to connect it.\n</code></pre> <p>Still arranging API access? Ask Plugin Creator to use sample data for now.</p> <h3 id=\"2-connect-your-system\">2. Connect your system</h3> <p>In the same conversation, ask Plugin Creator to connect the server to your system's API and walk you through sign-in. Use your organization's approved authentication method, and keep passwords, API keys, and other secrets out of chat.</p> <p>Need help? Send the Plugin Creator conversation and API documentation to your system owner or developer so they can help set up access.</p> <p><a id=\"connection-and-hosting-details\"></a> <strong>Connection and hosting details</strong></p> <p>Sites handles sign-in between ChatGPT and your MCP server. Your server still needs an approved connection to your system's API, which controls the records and actions it can access.</p> <p>For another host, follow <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/plugins/build/mcp-server.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Build an MCP server</a>, then <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/plugins/deploy/connect-chatgpt.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Connect and test your plugin</a>. See the <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/plugins/build/auth.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">authentication guide</a> for sign-in setup.</p> <h3 id=\"3-publish-and-install\">3. Publish and install</h3> <p>Ask Plugin Creator to publish the server with Sites and give you the plugin link, keeping your current access settings. The <a href=\"#/article/a-fc9cd7880ec6ce59?anchor=collaborate-on-a-site\">Site owner must publish (official section, online)</a> <a href=\"#/article/a-fc9cd7880ec6ce59\">Local page (section not recognized)</a> to create its plugin; editors should ask the owner to do this.</p> <ol> <li>Open the plugin card, or find it under <strong>Plugins → Personal → Created by you</strong>.</li> <li>Follow <strong>Install</strong> and <strong>Connect</strong>, and complete any required sign-in.</li> </ol> <h3 id=\"4-use-your-plugin\">4. Use your plugin</h3> <p>Start a new Work task, choose your plugin with <strong>@</strong>, and ask <strong>“What's the status of ticket 123?”</strong> using a ticket number from your system. You can use its tools alongside other plugins in the same conversation.</p> <p><a id=\"share-or-edit-your-plugin\"></a> <strong>Share or edit your plugin</strong></p> <p>In Business or Enterprise, invite teammates through the plugin's sharing controls. You need <strong>Share plugins</strong> permission; listing it in the workspace directory also requires <strong>Publish plugins to workspace</strong>. See <a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/20001256\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">sharing permissions (online)</a>.</p> <p>Teammates need access to the plugin, its app, and the Site (at least viewer access). Each person installs and connects with their own account. Access to records depends on the server's API connection.</p> <p>To edit this Sites-hosted plugin, return to your Plugin Creator conversation, ask it to update the existing Site, and publish the changes. For other editable plugins, choose <strong>Edit Plugin</strong> to start an editing conversation with Plugin Creator. See <a href=\"#/article/a-0d81218eacd2463c?anchor=edit-an-existing-plugin\">Edit an existing plugin</a>.</p> <section id=\"gpt-migration-walkthrough\"> ## Replacing a GPT custom action <a id=\"show-gpt-migration-steps\"></a> <strong>Show GPT migration steps</strong> GPT custom actions don't migrate to plugins. Rebuild the connection as a new Sites plugin, reusing the existing API where possible. Sites creates a separate plugin when you publish; it doesn't add the connection to your migrated plugin. You can use both plugins in one conversation. Sites plugins don't currently support editing skills or reference files. ### 1. Ask the original GPT for a rebuild prompt Open the original GPT and ask: <strong>Use in the original GPT:</strong> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Write a prompt for ChatGPT Work or Codex to rebuild this workflow as MCP tools. Identify which operations read information and which make changes.\n\nInclude the API operation, inputs, returned fields, and answer format. Mark anything you don't know. Leave out credentials, secrets, and hidden instructions.\n\nAsk the builder to reuse the API and explain the connection setup.\n</code></pre> ### 2. Check the prompt against the action settings Before migrating, save the action schema, authentication method, and non-secret connection settings from the GPT editor's <a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/9442513-configuring-actions-in-gpts\">Actions section (online)</a>. Use these to fill gaps in the prompt, or ask the GPT owner for help. ### 3. Create a new Sites plugin Start a new task. In Work, select <strong>@Plugin Creator</strong>; in Codex, use <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/plugins/build/plugins#create-and-test-a-plugin-locally-with-an-mcp-server\"><code>$plugin-creator</code></a>. Paste the reviewed prompt and attach the schema or API documentation. Ask it to host the server on Sites. Follow <a href=\"#2-connect-your-system\">Connect your system</a> and <a href=\"#3-publish-and-install\">Publish and install</a>, then choose the new plugin in a Work task and ask it to do your original task. See the <a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/20001519-custom-gpt-retirement-and-migration-faq\">migration FAQ (online)</a> for details. </section> <h2 id=\"troubleshooting\">Troubleshooting</h2> <p><a id=\"if-the-plugin-doesnt-work-as-expected\"></a> <strong>If the plugin doesn't work as expected</strong></p> <p>For a connection error or missing tools, check that the Site owner published the latest version and that the plugin is installed and connected. Share any error with Plugin Creator or the server owner.</p> <p>If ChatGPT doesn't use the tool, choose the plugin with <strong>@</strong> and ask for a specific lookup. If a teammate can't use it, check their plugin, app, Site, and record access.</p> <p>If the plugin is marked <strong>Desktop only</strong>, use a supported desktop app or ask the author to review its <a href=\"#/article/a-ab115ea47731f92a\">packaging</a>. A remote MCP server alone doesn't make a plugin web-compatible.</p> <h2 id=\"connect-an-existing-mcp-server\">Connect an existing MCP server</h2> <p>ChatGPT web uses remote MCP tools through plugins. If you already have a server, follow <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/plugins/deploy/connect-chatgpt.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Connect and test your plugin</a>. Local Codex clients can also connect directly to MCP servers and share their configuration.</p> <p>Choose your surface to see its setup and configuration options.</p> <p><a id=\"supported-mcp-features\"></a></p> <blockquote> <p><strong>Surface: app,cli,ide</strong></p> </blockquote> <p>The ChatGPT desktop app, Codex CLI, and IDE extension support MCP servers and share MCP configuration for the same Codex host.</p> <p>The supported server features below apply to MCP servers configured on a Codex host. Hosted plugin tools can have different capabilities.</p> <h2 id=\"supported-mcp-features\">Supported MCP features</h2> <ul> <li><strong>STDIO servers</strong>: Servers that run as a local process (started by a command).</li> <li>Environment variables</li> <li><strong>Streamable HTTP servers</strong>: Servers that you access at an address.</li> <li>Bearer token authentication</li> <li>OAuth authentication, including Client ID Metadata Documents (CIMD) and Dynamic Client Registration (DCR)</li> <li>ChatGPT session authentication for trusted first-party servers</li> <li><strong>Server instructions</strong>: Codex reads the MCP <code>instructions</code> field returned during initialization and uses it as server-wide guidance alongside the server's tools.</li> </ul> <p>If you build or maintain an MCP server for Codex, use <code>instructions</code> for cross-tool workflows, constraints, and rate limits that apply across the server. Keep the first 512 characters self-contained so the most important guidance is available when Codex is deciding how to use the server.</p> <h2 id=\"connect-codex-to-an-mcp-server\">Connect Codex to an MCP server</h2> <p>Codex stores MCP configuration in <code>config.toml</code> alongside other Codex configuration settings. By default this is <code>~/.codex/config.toml</code>, but you can also scope MCP servers to a project with <code>.codex/config.toml</code> (trusted projects only).</p> <p>The ChatGPT desktop app, Codex CLI, and IDE extension share this configuration. Once you configure your MCP servers, you can switch among those clients without redoing setup.</p> <blockquote> <p><strong>Surface: app</strong></p> </blockquote> <h3 id=\"configure-in-the-chatgpt-desktop-app\">Configure in the ChatGPT desktop app</h3> <ol> <li>Open <strong>Settings</strong>, then select <strong>MCP servers</strong>.</li> <li>Select <strong>Add server</strong>.</li> <li>Enter a name, choose <strong>STDIO</strong> or <strong>Streamable HTTP</strong>, and provide the server's command or URL.</li> <li>Save the server, then select <strong>Restart</strong>.</li> </ol> <p>The server list shows which servers are enabled and which require OAuth. Select <strong>Authenticate</strong> when an OAuth server requires sign-in. In the composer, type <code>/mcp</code> to view connected servers.</p> <blockquote> <p><strong>Surface: web</strong></p> </blockquote> <h2 id=\"use-mcp-backed-tools-in-chatgpt-web\">Use MCP-backed tools in ChatGPT web</h2> <p>Continuing a conversation using Local computer access with Work Cloud on another device doesn't install plugins or grant access to connected accounts.</p> <p>In Local computer access with Work Cloud, the enterprise <code>mcp_servers</code> TOML requirement in Agent Security applies to local executors. Cloud containers retain Work Cloud policies. Local MCP servers and transports may not be available in the cloud; check connectivity and authentication separately.</p> <p>For enterprise hooks in Local computer access with Work Cloud:</p> <ul> <li><strong>Enterprise hooks.</strong> Where enabled for your workspace, Local computer access with Work Cloud supports admin-defined MCP hooks that run on the cloud coordinator (orchestrator) for supported lifecycle and tool events. Command hooks and hooks from local configuration or plugins are not supported with cloud orchestration, even when tools execute locally.</li> <li><strong>Auditing.</strong> Before relying on these hooks, test the callback connection, confirm the events it receives, and check how failures affect the task. MCP hooks do not provide a complete Compliance API audit trail.</li> <li><strong>Limitations:</strong> Command hooks and hooks from local configuration or plugins are not supported with cloud orchestration, even when tools execute locally. Consumers do not have hooks support in this feature. When both orchestration and execution are local, existing supported hooks continue to work in local-only Work and Codex threads. Admins can still configure supported managed hooks in Agent Security for those workflows.</li> </ul> <p>See <a href=\"#/article/a-0aecdb1ef0cec0a4\">Hooks</a> and the <a href=\"#/article/a-c2332644faa13713\">Configuration Reference</a> for support scope.</p> <p>In a hosted ChatGPT Work chat, install a <a href=\"#/article/a-dea5d8982f047a3a\">plugin</a> to use its bundled connectors and remote MCP tools. After installation, Chat and Work can use those tools. Workspace administrators can control which plugins and tools are available.</p> <p>ChatGPT web doesn't read local Codex configuration files or expose the local Codex command menu. Open the <strong>Plugins</strong> tab to browse and manage available tools.</p> <blockquote> <p><strong>Surface: cli</strong></p> </blockquote> <h3 id=\"configure-with-the-cli\">Configure with the CLI</h3> <h4 id=\"add-an-mcp-server\">Add an MCP server</h4> <pre><code class=\"language-bash\">codex mcp add &lt;server-name&gt; --env VAR1=VALUE1 --env VAR2=VALUE2 -- &lt;stdio server-command&gt;\n</code></pre> <p>For example, to add Context7 (a free MCP server for developer documentation), you can run the following command:</p> <pre><code class=\"language-bash\">codex mcp add context7 -- npx -y @upstash/context7-mcp\n</code></pre> <h4 id=\"other-cli-commands\">Other CLI commands</h4> <p>Run <code>codex mcp list</code> to see configured servers. To see all available MCP commands, run <code>codex mcp --help</code>. For a server that supports OAuth, run <code>codex mcp login &lt;server-name&gt;</code>.</p> <h4 id=\"terminal-ui-tui\">Terminal UI (TUI)</h4> <p>In the <code>codex</code> TUI, use <code>/mcp</code> to see your active MCP servers.</p> <blockquote> <p><strong>Surface: ide</strong></p> </blockquote> <h3 id=\"configure-in-the-ide-extension\">Configure in the IDE extension</h3> <ol> <li>Open the gear menu, then select <strong>MCP servers</strong>.</li> <li>Select <strong>Add server</strong>.</li> <li>Enter a name, choose <strong>STDIO</strong> or <strong>Streamable HTTP</strong>, and provide the server's command or URL.</li> <li>Save the server, then select <strong>Restart extension</strong>.</li> </ol> <p>The MCP server list shows which servers are enabled and which require OAuth. Select <strong>Authenticate</strong> when an OAuth server requires sign-in.</p> <blockquote> <p><strong>Surface: app,cli,ide</strong></p> </blockquote> <h3 id=\"configure-with-configtoml\">Configure with config.toml</h3> <p>For more fine-grained control, edit <code>~/.codex/config.toml</code> or a project-scoped <code>.codex/config.toml</code>. See the <a href=\"#/article/a-c2332644faa13713\">configuration reference</a> for a searchable list of every supported MCP option.</p> <p>Configure each MCP server with a <code>[mcp_servers.&lt;server-name&gt;]</code> table in the configuration file.</p> <p><a id=\"stdio-servers\"></a></p> <blockquote> <p><strong>Surface: app,cli,ide</strong></p> </blockquote> <h4 id=\"stdio-servers\">STDIO servers</h4> <ul> <li><code>command</code> (required): The command that starts the server.</li> <li><code>args</code> (optional): Arguments to pass to the server.</li> <li><code>env</code> (optional): Environment variables to set for the server.</li> <li><code>env_vars</code> (optional): Environment variables to allow and forward.</li> <li><code>cwd</code> (optional): Working directory to start the server from.</li> <li><code>experimental_environment</code> (optional): Set to <code>remote</code> to start the stdio server through a remote executor environment when one is available.</li> </ul> <p><code>env_vars</code> can contain plain variable names or objects with a source:</p> <pre><code class=\"language-toml\">env_vars = [\"LOCAL_TOKEN\", { name = \"REMOTE_TOKEN\", source = \"remote\" }]\n</code></pre> <p>String entries and <code>source = \"local\"</code> read from Codex's local environment. <code>source = \"remote\"</code> reads from the remote executor environment and requires remote MCP stdio.</p> <p><a id=\"streamable-http-servers\"></a></p> <blockquote> <p><strong>Surface: app,cli,ide</strong></p> </blockquote> <h4 id=\"streamable-http-servers\">Streamable HTTP servers</h4> <ul> <li><code>url</code> (required): The server address.</li> <li><code>auth</code> (optional): Authentication to try after configured bearer tokens and authorization headers. Use <code>oauth</code> (the default) for stored MCP OAuth credentials. Use <code>chatgpt</code> to use the current ChatGPT session for the trusted first-party ChatGPT origin, with stored OAuth as a fallback.</li> <li><code>bearer_token_env_var</code> (optional): Environment variable name for a bearer token to send in <code>Authorization</code>.</li> <li><code>http_headers</code> (optional): Map of header names to static values.</li> <li><code>env_http_headers</code> (optional): Map of header names to environment variable names (values pulled from the environment).</li> <li><code>http_headers_helper</code> (optional): Local command that prints a JSON object of header names and string values, such as <code>{\"X-Auth\": \"temporary-token\"}</code>. Supported for HTTP MCP connections made from the local environment; not for stdio servers or connections made through a remote execution environment.</li> </ul> <p>Codex caches helper headers for the connection. After a same-origin POST returns <code>401</code> or <code>403</code>, it refreshes the headers once and retries only if the helper returns changed values. Explicit bearer tokens and OAuth credentials take precedence over a helper-provided <code>Authorization</code> header. An OAuth <code>403</code> response that reports insufficient scope doesn't trigger a helper refresh.</p> <p>If no credential source resolves, Codex can connect to the server without authentication. Run <code>codex mcp login &lt;server-name&gt;</code> separately to start an MCP OAuth login.</p> <h4 id=\"other-configuration-options\">Other configuration options</h4> <ul> <li><code>startup_timeout_sec</code> (optional): Timeout (seconds) for the server to start. Default: <code>10</code>.</li> <li><code>tool_timeout_sec</code> (optional): Timeout (seconds) for the server to run a tool. Default: <code>60</code>.</li> <li><code>enabled</code> (optional): Set <code>false</code> to disable a server without deleting it.</li> <li><code>required</code> (optional): Set <code>true</code> to make startup fail if this enabled server can't initialize.</li> <li><code>enabled_tools</code> (optional): Tool allow list.</li> <li><code>disabled_tools</code> (optional): Tool deny list (applied after <code>enabled_tools</code>).</li> <li><code>default_tools_approval_mode</code> (optional): Default approval behavior for tools from this server. Supported values are <code>auto</code>, <code>prompt</code>, <code>writes</code>, and <code>approve</code>. The <code>writes</code> mode prompts for tools that aren't marked read-only.</li> <li><code>tools.&lt;tool&gt;.approval_mode</code> (optional): Per-tool approval behavior override.</li> <li><code>tools.&lt;tool&gt;.output_token_limit</code> (optional): Positive token budget for one tool's output, before the standard 20% serialization allowance. Overrides the model's default output truncation budget for that tool.</li> </ul> <p>The top-level <code>mcp_optional_startup_grace_ms</code> setting controls how long Codex waits for optional MCP servers when building the initial tool catalog. It defaults to <code>1000</code> milliseconds. Set it to <code>0</code> to wait for each server's <code>startup_timeout_sec</code> instead. Required servers still use their startup timeouts.</p> <h4 id=\"oauth-client-registration-and-callbacks\">OAuth client registration and callbacks</h4> <p>When your authorization server requires a pre-registered OAuth client, provide its client ID when adding the MCP server:</p> <pre><code class=\"language-bash\">codex mcp add example --url https://mcp.example.com --oauth-client-id my-client\n</code></pre> <p>For a confidential client, also pass <code>--oauth-client-secret</code>. Read the secret from an environment variable:</p> <pre><code class=\"language-bash\">codex mcp add example --url https://mcp.example.com --oauth-client-id my-client --oauth-client-secret \"$MCP_CLIENT_SECRET\"\n</code></pre> <p>This option requires a nonempty client ID and secret. Codex saves the secret as <code>mcp_servers.example.oauth.client_secret</code> in <code>config.toml</code>. Keep that file private and out of version control.</p> <p>Codex displays the complete callback URL to register with your provider:</p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">OAuth callback URL: http://127.0.0.1/callback\n</code></pre> <p>Codex saves the callback alongside the client ID in <code>config.toml</code> for later logins:</p> <pre><code class=\"language-toml\">[mcp_servers.example]\nurl = \"https://mcp.example.com\"\n\n[mcp_servers.example.oauth]\nclient_id = \"my-client\"\ncallback_url = \"http://127.0.0.1/callback\"\n</code></pre> <p>Newly added pre-registered clients use a stable callback only when the authorization server advertises <code>authorization_response_iss_parameter_supported: true</code> and provides a metadata <code>issuer</code>. If issuer support isn't advertised, Codex appends a server-specific callback ID, such as <code>http://127.0.0.1/callback/XuuuHAzzHOni</code>. Existing clients without a saved callback continue using their callback-ID-specific redirect.</p> <p>During login, callback selection depends on the OAuth configuration and authorization server metadata:</p> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>OAuth configuration</th> <th>Issuer support</th> <th>Callback used</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td><code>callback_url</code> without <code>client_id</code></td> <td>Supported</td> <td>The configured callback is used for client registration.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>callback_url</code> without <code>client_id</code></td> <td>Unsupported</td> <td>The configured callback is used for client registration with the server-specific callback ID appended.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>client_id</code> and <code>callback_url</code></td> <td>Supported</td> <td>The configured callback is reused; the authorization response must contain the matching <code>iss</code>.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>client_id</code> and a <code>callback_url</code> ending in the correct callback ID</td> <td>Unsupported</td> <td>The configured callback is reused unchanged.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>client_id</code> and a <code>callback_url</code> missing the correct callback ID</td> <td>Unsupported</td> <td>The configured callback is ignored. Codex uses <code>mcp_oauth_callback_url</code>, or <code>http://127.0.0.1/callback</code> when unset, with the callback ID appended.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>client_id</code> without a configured <code>callback_url</code></td> <td>Supported or unsupported</td> <td>Codex uses the global or default callback with the server-specific callback ID appended.</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p>The fallback doesn't modify the stored callback URL. Codex derives the callback ID from the MCP server URL, including its path and query string. The same selection rules apply to automatic and explicit login.</p> <p>Set <code>mcp_oauth_callback_url</code> when you need a custom callback path or remote Devbox ingress URL. Newly added pre-registered clients use that URL unchanged when their provider supports issuer identification. Otherwise, they use the configured URL with the server-specific callback ID appended. Always register the exact callback displayed by <code>codex mcp add</code>.</p> <p>For <code>http://127.0.0.1</code> callbacks without an explicit port, Codex omits the listener port from the URL it displays and stores, then inserts the active listener port during authorization. This substitution doesn't apply to <code>localhost</code>, IPv6 hosts, HTTPS URLs, or callbacks that already include a port. Authorization servers must accept variable loopback ports under <a href=\"https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8252#section-7.3\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">RFC 8252, Section 7.3 (online)</a>.</p> <p>Set <code>mcp_oauth_callback_port</code> to choose a fixed global listener port, or set <code>mcp_servers.&lt;server-name&gt;.oauth.callback_port</code> to override it for one server. An explicit port in the callback URL doesn't configure the listener. For a direct loopback callback, use <code>http://127.0.0.1</code> without an explicit port or configure the same explicit port for both the callback URL and listener. A proxied callback can intentionally use an external URL port that differs from the local listener port. Local callback URLs bind to the local interface; non-local callback URLs bind to <code>0.0.0.0</code>.</p> <p>Codex validates any returned <code>iss</code> before exchanging the authorization code. A mismatched <code>iss</code> always rejects the response. When issuer support is advertised, a missing <code>iss</code> also rejects it. Neither failure exchanges the code or falls back to another callback. A malformed callback URL or issuer support advertised without a metadata issuer also remains a hard failure. See <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/plugins/build/auth.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Authenticate users</a>.</p> <p>If the MCP server advertises <code>scopes_supported</code>, Codex prefers those server-advertised scopes during OAuth login. Otherwise, Codex falls back to the scopes configured in <code>config.toml</code>.</p> <h4 id=\"oauth-client-registration\">OAuth client registration</h4> <p>Codex supports <a href=\"https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/draft-ietf-oauth-client-id-metadata-document/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">OAuth Client ID Metadata Documents (CIMD) (online)</a> and Dynamic Client Registration (DCR). By default, Codex automatically chooses CIMD when the authorization server advertises <code>client_id_metadata_document_supported: true</code>, includes <code>none</code> in <code>token_endpoint_auth_methods_supported</code>, and the callback uses a supported loopback URL. Otherwise, Codex uses DCR when available. A configured OAuth client ID always takes precedence and skips client registration.</p> <p>For CIMD without issuer-bound responses, Codex CLI uses a ChatGPT-hosted metadata document specific to the MCP server:</p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">https://chatgpt.com/oauth/codex/&lt;callback_id&gt;/client.json\n</code></pre> <p>Codex derives <code>&lt;callback_id&gt;</code> from the MCP server URL and includes it in the loopback redirect URI, such as <code>http://127.0.0.1:&lt;port&gt;/callback/&lt;callback_id&gt;</code>. The metadata document registers the matching loopback URI without a port. Authorization servers must accept the port selected at login while matching the host and path exactly, as required by <a href=\"https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8252.html#section-7.3\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">RFC 8252 (online)</a>. Custom callback hosts, paths, or query parameters require DCR or a configured OAuth client ID.</p> <p>Codex CLI also supports a stable, shared CIMD document:</p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">https://chatgpt.com/oauth/codex/client.json\n</code></pre> <p>Codex CLI uses the stable document with the shared <code>/callback</code> path when the authorization server advertises <code>authorization_response_iss_parameter_supported: true</code>, provides a valid <code>issuer</code> in its metadata, and includes a matching <code>iss</code> in authorization responses. Servers without issuer-bound responses use the callback-specific document.</p> <p>To choose a registration method for one CLI login, use <code>--oauth-client-registration</code>:</p> <pre><code class=\"language-bash\">codex mcp login &lt;server-name&gt; --oauth-client-registration cimd\ncodex mcp login &lt;server-name&gt; --oauth-client-registration dcr\n</code></pre> <p>The default is <code>auto</code>. Registration choices apply only to the current login and aren't stored in <code>config.toml</code>.</p> <h4 id=\"configtoml-examples\">config.toml examples</h4> <pre><code class=\"language-toml\">[mcp_servers.context7]\ncommand = \"npx\"\nargs = [\"-y\", \"@upstash/context7-mcp\"]\nenv_vars = [\"LOCAL_TOKEN\"]\n\n[mcp_servers.context7.env]\nMY_ENV_VAR = \"MY_ENV_VALUE\"\n</code></pre> <pre><code class=\"language-toml\"># Optional MCP OAuth callback overrides (used by `codex mcp login`)\nmcp_oauth_callback_port = 5555\nmcp_oauth_callback_url = \"https://devbox.example.internal/callback\"\n</code></pre> <pre><code class=\"language-toml\">[mcp_servers.figma]\nurl = \"https://mcp.figma.com/mcp\"\nbearer_token_env_var = \"FIGMA_OAUTH_TOKEN\"\nhttp_headers = { \"X-Figma-Region\" = \"us-east-1\" }\n</code></pre> <pre><code class=\"language-toml\">[mcp_servers.chrome_devtools]\nurl = \"http://localhost:3000/mcp\"\nenabled_tools = [\"open\", \"screenshot\"]\ndisabled_tools = [\"screenshot\"] # applied after enabled_tools\ndefault_tools_approval_mode = \"prompt\"\nstartup_timeout_sec = 20\ntool_timeout_sec = 45\nenabled = true\n\n[mcp_servers.chrome_devtools.tools.open]\napproval_mode = \"approve\"\noutput_token_limit = 30000\n</code></pre> <h3 id=\"plugin-provided-mcp-servers\">Plugin-provided MCP servers</h3> <p>Installed plugins can bundle MCP servers in their plugin manifest. Those servers are launched from the plugin, so user config doesn't set their transport command. User config can still control on/off state and tool policy under <code>plugins.&lt;plugin&gt;.mcp_servers.&lt;server&gt;</code>.</p> <pre><code class=\"language-toml\">[plugins.\"sample@test\".mcp_servers.sample]\nenabled = true\ndefault_tools_approval_mode = \"prompt\"\nenabled_tools = [\"read\", \"search\"]\n\n[plugins.\"sample@test\".mcp_servers.sample.tools.search]\napproval_mode = \"approve\"\n</code></pre> <p>Plugin-provided HTTP MCP servers can also declare OAuth settings in <code>.mcp.json</code>. Plugin manifests use the camelCase field names <code>clientId</code>, <code>callbackUrl</code>, and <code>callbackPort</code>:</p> <pre><code class=\"language-json\">{\n  \"mcpServers\": {\n    \"sample\": {\n      \"type\": \"http\",\n      \"url\": \"https://mcp.example.com/mcp\",\n      \"oauth\": {\n        \"clientId\": \"my-pre-registered-client\",\n        \"callbackUrl\": \"http://127.0.0.1/callback/registered\"\n      }\n    }\n  }\n}\n</code></pre> <p>Plugin-provided MCP servers follow the same callback-selection rules as other MCP servers. If a plugin provides a <code>clientId</code>, its provider doesn't support issuer-bound callbacks, and <code>callbackUrl</code> lacks the server-specific callback ID, Codex ignores that URL for the login and uses <code>mcp_oauth_callback_url</code>, or <code>http://127.0.0.1/callback</code> when unset, with the callback ID appended. The configured <code>callbackUrl</code> remains unchanged.</p> <p>A plugin's <code>oauth.callbackPort</code> overrides the global <code>mcp_oauth_callback_port</code>; if neither is set, Codex chooses an ephemeral port. The port embedded in <code>callbackUrl</code> doesn't select the listener port. For a direct loopback callback with a fixed port, configure both values to match:</p> <pre><code class=\"language-json\">{\n  \"callbackUrl\": \"http://127.0.0.1:4321/callback/registered\",\n  \"callbackPort\": 4321\n}\n</code></pre> <p>For remote ingress or another proxy, the callback URL port and local listener port can intentionally differ when the proxy forwards to the configured listener.</p> <h2 id=\"examples-of-useful-mcp-servers\">Examples of useful MCP servers</h2> <p>The list of MCP servers keeps growing. Here are a few common ones:</p> <ul> <li><a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/learn/docs-mcp.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">OpenAI Docs MCP</a>: Search and read OpenAI developer docs.</li> <li><a href=\"https://github.com/upstash/context7\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Context7 (online)</a>: Connect to up-to-date developer documentation.</li> <li>Figma <a href=\"https://developers.figma.com/docs/figma-mcp-server/local-server-installation/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Local (online)</a> and <a href=\"https://developers.figma.com/docs/figma-mcp-server/remote-server-installation/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Remote (online)</a>: Access your Figma designs.</li> <li><a href=\"https://www.npmjs.com/package/@playwright/mcp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Playwright (online)</a>: Control and inspect a browser using Playwright.</li> <li><a href=\"https://github.com/ChromeDevTools/chrome-devtools-mcp/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Chrome Developer Tools (online)</a>: Control and inspect Chrome.</li> <li><a href=\"https://docs.sentry.io/product/sentry-mcp/#codex\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Sentry (online)</a>: Access Sentry logs.</li> <li><a href=\"https://github.com/github/github-mcp-server\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">GitHub (online)</a>: Manage GitHub beyond what <code>git</code> supports (for example, pull requests and issues).</li> </ul>"};
